.\" What a stern warning against even missing the correct time of salaat, as (according to this quotation) to miss the correct time of salaat is to discard it. Although, according to the interpretation of the Ulama, the verdict of kufr is given against a person only when he rejects (and not simply neglects) salaat, yet the words of the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) occurring in these ahaadith should be very weighty for those who have any regard for him. It may, however, be noted that some of the very important companions of the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) like Umar, Abdullah bin Mas''ood, Abdullah bin Abbas (Radhiyallaho anhum), etc. and eminent jurists like Ahmad bin Hanbal, Ishaaq bin Raahwayh, Ibn Mubaarak, (Rahmatullah alaihim), etc. are definitely of the opinion that verdict of kufr can be given against the person who intentionally discards his salaat. May Allah save us!", "rawOcrText": "34 Virtues of Salaat is cloudy (lest you should err and miss the correct time), for to discard salaat is to become a kaafir.\" What a *ern warning against even missing the correct time of salaat, as (according to this quotation) to miss the correct time of salaat is to discard it. Although, according to the interpreta- tion of the Ulama, the verdict of kufr is given against a person only when he rejects (and not simply neglects) salaat, yet •the words of the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wa- sallam) occurring in these ahaadith should be very weighty for those who. have any regard for him. It may, however, be noted that some of the very important companions of the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) like Umar, Abdullah bin Mas''ood, Abdullah bin Abbas (Radhiyallaho anhum), etc. and eminent jurists like Ahmad bin Hanbal, Ishaaq bin Raahwayh, Ibn Mubaarak, (Rahmatullah alaihim), etc. are definitely of the opinion that verdict of kufr can be given against the person who intentionally discards his salaat. May Allah save us! Hadith—II J\" Jij Hadhrat Ubaadah bin Saamit (Radhiyallaho anho) nar- rates. ''My dear friend the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) while enjoining upon me seven good prac- tices said, \"Do not ascribe anything as partner to Allah, though you may be cut into pieces or burnt alive or crucified; do not forego salaat intentionally, lest you should get out of the fold of Islam; do not perpetrate disobedience of Allah, lest you deserve His wrath; and do not take to drinking, for that is the mother of all In anothå hadith, Hadhrat Abu Darda (Radhiyallaho anho) says, \"My dear Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) warned me saying, ''Do not ascribe anything as partner unto", "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0340000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "sequenceIndex": 1, "blockType": "heading", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadith.—II", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0340000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "sequenceIndex": 2, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "عَنْ عُبَادَةَ بْنِ الصَّامِتِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ أَوْصَانِي خَلِيلِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ بِسَبْعِ خِصَالٍ فَقَالَ لَا تُشْرِكُوا بِاللَّهِ شَيْئًا وَإِنْ قُطِّعْتُمْ أَوْ حُرِّقْتُمْ وَلَا تَتْرُكُوا الصَّلَاةَ مُتَعَمِّدِينَ فَمَنْ تَرَكَهَا مُتَعَمِّدًا فَقَدْ خَرَجَ مِنَ الْمِلَّةِ وَلَا تَرْكَبُوا الْمَعْصِيَةَ فَإِنَّهَا سَخَطُ اللَّهِ وَلَا تَشْرَبُوا الْخَمْرَ فَإِنَّهَا رَأْسُ الْخَطَايَا", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0340000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "sequenceIndex": 3, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "رواه الطبراني ومحمد بن نصر في كتاب الصلاة بإسنادين لا بأس بهما كذا في الترغيب هكذا ذكره السيوطي في الدر المنثور وعزاه إليهما وفي المشكاة برواية ابن ماجه عن ابن أبي الدرداء نحوه", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0340000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "sequenceIndex": 4, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Ubaadah bin Saamit (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates: ''My dear friend the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) while enjoining upon me seven good practices said, \"Do not ascribe anything as partner to Allah, though you may be cut into pieces or burnt alive or crucified; do not forego salaat intentionally, lest you should get out of the fold of Islam; do not perpetrate disobedience of Allah, lest you deserve His wrath; and do not take to drinking, for that is the mother of all In another hadith, Hadhrat Abu Darda (Radhiyallaho anho) says, \"My dear Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) warned me saying, ''Do not ascribe anything as partner unto", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}], "pageNumber": 34}'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO temp_import_pages VALUES ('{"pageId": "c0350000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "bookPartId": "59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7", "sourceShowsPrintedPageLabel": true, "printedPageLabel": "35", "printedPageNumber": 35, "pdfPageNumber": 418, "sequenceIndex": 25, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "scanLanguages": ["en", "ar"], "reviewEvidence": {"englishTranscriptionComplete": true, "arabicTranscriptionComplete": true, "blockOrderChecked": true, "identifiersChecked": true, "scanCompared": true, "provenanceNotes": "Canonical transcription checked against the rendered secondary scan; master PDF page mapping retained. Fine vocalisation is preserved where clearly legible; no unresolved Arabic word or letter remains. English OCR correction and Arabic/translation-pair classification pass compared against the rendered source scan; raw OCR retained unchanged."}, "structuralNodes": [{"id": "a6000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "parentId": null, "nodeType": "section", "sourceLabel": "PART I", "sourceIdentifier": "I", "title": "IMPORTANCE OF SALAAT", "sequenceIndex": 0, "startPageId": null, "endPageId": null}, {"id": "a6100000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "parentId": "a6000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "nodeType": "chapter", "sourceLabel": "CHAPTER.—II", "sourceIdentifier": "II", "title": "WARNING AND REPROACH FOR NEGLECTING SALAAT", "sequenceIndex": 1, "startPageId": null, "endPageId": null}, {"id": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003", "parentId": "a6100000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "nodeType": "hadith", "sourceLabel": "Hadith-III", "sourceIdentifier": "III", "title": null, "sequenceIndex": 2, "startPageId": null, "endPageId": null}], "blocks": [{"id": "d0350000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003", "sequenceIndex": 0, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Allah, though you may cut into pieces or burnt alive or crucified; do not discard salaat intentionally, as Allah is free from any obligation to a person who knowingly neglects salaat; and do not take wine, for that is the key to all vices.\"", "rawOcrText": "Part I on Discard of Salaat 35 Allah, though you may cut into pieces or burnt alive or crucified; do not discard salaat intentionally, as Allah is free from any obligation to a person who knowingly neg- lects salaat; and do not take wine, for that is the key to all viæs.\" Hadith-m Jij g Jj; J:aji Jj & e; t''*$ 3i ji 8.i g:ij by Hadhrat Mu''aaz bin Jabal (Radhiyallaho anho) nar- rates: \"The Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) en- joined upon me ten things, viz, ''Do not ascribe anything is partner unto Allah, though you may be slain or burnt alive; do not disobey your parents, though you may have to part with your wife or your entire wealth; do not neglect fardh salaat, intention- ally, for Allah is free from •obligation to a person who neglects fardh salaat intentionally; do not take wine, for it is an evil habit; that is the root of every vice; do not commit disobedience of Allah, for that brings the wrath of Allah. Do not turn your back to the enemy in battle, though all your comrades may have •fallen. Do nbt fly from the locality where an epidemic has broken out. Do spend on your family members according to your capacity; let your rod be hanging on them, as a warning. and to chastise against neglect of their duties towards Allah.\" According to this hadith, we should not spare the rod in checking the children from becoming reckless in• doing anything they like. Sometimes it is necessary to use the rod. It is a pity that out of love we do not use the rod in the beginning and, when the children get spoilt,. we cry and", "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0350000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003", "sequenceIndex": 1, "blockType": "heading", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadith-III", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0350000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003", "sequenceIndex": 2, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "عَنْ مُعَاذِ بْنِ جَبَلٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ أَوْصَانِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ ﷺ بِعَشْرِ كَلِمَاتٍ قَالَ لَا تُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ شَيْئًا وَإِنْ قُتِلْتَ أَوْ حُرِّقْتَ وَلَا تَعُقَّنَّ وَالِدَيْكَ وَإِنْ أَمَرَاكَ أَنْ تَخْرُجَ مِنْ أَهْلِكَ وَمَالِكَ وَلَا تَتْرُكَنَّ صَلَاةً مَكْتُوبَةً مُتَعَمِّدًا فَإِنَّ مَنْ تَرَكَ صَلَاةً مَكْتُوبَةً مُتَعَمِّدًا فَقَدْ بَرِئَتْ مِنْهُ ذِمَّةُ اللَّهِ وَلَا تَشْرَبَنَّ خَمْرًا فَإِنَّهُ رَأْسُ كُلِّ فَاحِشَةٍ وَإِيَّاكَ وَالْمَعْصِيَةَ فَإِنَّ بِالْمَعْصِيَةِ حَلَّ سَخَطُ اللَّهِ وَإِيَّاكَ وَالْفِرَارَ مِنَ الزَّحْفِ وَإِنْ هَلَكَ النَّاسُ وَإِنْ أَصَابَ النَّاسَ مَوْتٌ وَأَنْتَ فِيهِمْ فَاثْبُتْ وَأَنْفِقْ عَلَى أَهْلِكَ مِنْ طَوْلِكَ وَلَا تَرْفَعْ عَنْهُمْ عَصَاكَ أَدَبًا وَأَخِفْهُمْ فِي اللَّهِ", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0350000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003", "sequenceIndex": 3, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "رواه أحمد والطبراني في الكبير وغيرهم", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0350000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003", "sequenceIndex": 4, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Mu''aaz bin Jabal (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates: \"The Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) enjoined upon me ten things, viz, ''Do not ascribe anything as partner unto Allah, though you may be slain or burnt alive; do not disobey your parents, though you may have to part with your wife or your entire wealth; do not neglect fardh salaat, intentionally, for Allah is free from obligation to a person who neglects fardh salaat intentionally; do not take wine, for it is an evil habit; that is the root of every vice; do not commit disobedience of Allah, for that brings the wrath of Allah. Do not turn your back to the enemy in battle, though all your comrades may have fallen. Do not fly from the locality where an epidemic has broken out. Do spend on your family members according to your capacity; let your rod be hanging on them, as a warning. and to chastise against neglect of their duties towards Allah.\" According to this hadith, we should not spare the rod in checking the children from becoming reckless in doing anything they like. Sometimes it is necessary to use the rod. It is a pity that out of love we do not use the rod in the beginning and, when the children get spoilt, we cry and", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}], "pageNumber": 35}'::jsonb);
INSERT INTO temp_import_pages VALUES ('{"pageId": "c0360000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "bookPartId": "59d7f112-fb58-4726-9c35-11485c6155e7", "sourceShowsPrintedPageLabel": true, "printedPageLabel": "36", "printedPageNumber": 36, "pdfPageNumber": 419, "sequenceIndex": 26, "verificationStatus": "in_review", "scanLanguages": ["en", "ar"], "reviewEvidence": {"englishTranscriptionComplete": true, "arabicTranscriptionComplete": true, "blockOrderChecked": true, "identifiersChecked": true, "scanCompared": true, "provenanceNotes": "Canonical transcription checked against the rendered secondary scan; master PDF page mapping retained. Fine vocalisation is preserved where clearly legible; no unresolved Arabic word or letter remains. English OCR correction and Arabic/translation-pair classification pass compared against the rendered source scan; raw OCR retained unchanged."}, "structuralNodes": [{"id": "a6000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "parentId": null, "nodeType": "section", "sourceLabel": "PART I", "sourceIdentifier": "I", "title": "IMPORTANCE OF SALAAT", "sequenceIndex": 0, "startPageId": null, "endPageId": null}, {"id": "a6100000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "parentId": "a6000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "nodeType": "chapter", "sourceLabel": "CHAPTER.—II", "sourceIdentifier": "II", "title": "WARNING AND REPROACH FOR NEGLECTING SALAAT", "sequenceIndex": 1, "startPageId": null, "endPageId": null}, {"id": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004", "parentId": "a6100000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "nodeType": "hadith", "sourceLabel": "Hadith-IV", "sourceIdentifier": "IV", "title": null, "sequenceIndex": 2, "startPageId": null, "endPageId": null}], "blocks": [{"id": "d0360000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004", "sequenceIndex": 0, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "complain about them. To spare the rod and to spoil the child is no kindness at all. Who would like to save a child from a surgical operation under advice from a doctor for the simple reason that it would cause pain to him? The Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) is reported to have said very often: \"Enjoin salaat on your child when he is seven years old, and beat him if he neglects it after he reaches ten.\" Hadhrat Abdullah bin Mas''ood (Radhiyallaho anho) says, \"Guard the salaat of your children and inculcate good habits in them''). Luqmaan the wise used to say, \"The. use of the.rod on a child is as. indispensable as is water for the fields.\" The Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) is reported to have said, \"A person while admonishing his children earns more reward from Allah than when he is spending about seven pounds of grain in His path.\" In another hadith the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) has Said, \"May Allah bless a person who keeps a lash hanging in his house for the admonition of his house-folk.\" On another occasion he said, \"No father can bestow anything better on his children than to teach them good manners. \"", "rawOcrText": "36 Virtues of Salaat complain about them. To spare the rod and to spoil the child is no kindness at ill. Who would like to save a child from .d surgical operation under advice from a doctor for the simple reason that it would• cause pain to him? The Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) is reported to have said very often: \"Enjoin salaat on your child when he is seven years old, and beat him if he neglects it after he reaches ten.\" Hadhrat Abdullah bin Mas''ood (Radhiyallaho anho) says, \"Guard the salaat of your children and incul• cate good habits in them''). Luqmaan the wise used to say, \"The. use of the .rod on a child is as. indispensable as is water for the fields.\" The Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasal- lain) is reported to have said, \"A person while admonish: ing his children earns more reward from•Allah than when he is spending about seven pounds of grain in His path.\" In• another hadith the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) has Said, \"May Allah bless a person who keeps a lash hang- ing in his house for the admbnition of his house-folk.\" On another occasion he said, \"No father can bestow anything better on his children than to teach them good manners. \" Hadith-IV Lat Jul, us Li Hadhrat Naufil bin Mu''aawiyah (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates that he heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, \"A person who has missed one salaat is like one who has lost all his family and wealth.\" Salaat is missed usually when either •a person is in the company of his family members or is in pursuit of money. According to this hadith, the ultimate loss sustained in missing a salaat is in no way.less than the loss of the whole family and property. In other Words, if we miss a salaat we should be as much grieved as when we lose all of our folk and entire belongings. If we are cautioned by some reliable person about the presence of gangsters on a certain road, where people are robbed and killed during the night, we need a lion''s heart to the caution and travel on that road even during the day-time. Strange enough to note that", "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0360000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004", "sequenceIndex": 1, "blockType": "heading", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadith-IV", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0360000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004", "sequenceIndex": 2, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "عَنْ نَوْفَلِ بْنِ مُعَاوِيَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ ﷺ قَالَ مَنْ فَاتَتْهُ صَلَاةٌ فَكَأَنَّمَا وُتِرَ أَهْلُهُ وَمَالُهُ", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0360000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004", "sequenceIndex": 3, "blockType": "arabic", "languageCode": "ar", "direction": "rtl", "textContent": "رواه ابن حبان في صحيحه كذا في الترغيب زاد السيوطي في الدر والنسائي أيضا قلت ورواه أحمد في مسنده", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}, {"id": "d0360000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005", "structuralNodeId": "a6300000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004", "sequenceIndex": 4, "blockType": "english", "languageCode": "en", "direction": "ltr", "textContent": "Hadhrat Naufil bin Mu''aawiyah (Radhiyallaho anho) narrates that he heard the Prophet (Sallallaho alaihe wasallam) saying, \"A person who has missed one salaat is like one who has lost all his family and wealth.\" Salaat is missed usually when either a person is in the company of his family members or is in pursuit of money. According to this hadith, the ultimate loss sustained in missing a salaat is in no way less than the loss of the whole family and property. In other Words, if we miss a salaat we should be as much grieved as when we lose all of our folk and entire belongings. If we are cautioned by some reliable person about the presence of gangsters on a certain road, where people are robbed and killed during the night, we need a lion''s heart to the caution and travel on that road even during the day-time. Strange enough to note that", "rawOcrText": null, "ttsEligible": true, "verificationStatus": "in_review"}], "pageNumber": 36}'::jsonb);
